    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. There's a single test in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`) and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence number entirely, and propagated that change to everything derived from it.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.customerCode(Owner)`** \u2014 replaced the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` builder with:\n- **REGION** = `cityRegionResolver.regionFor(city, postcode)` (region code derived from the postcode, falling back to city)\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, reusing the existing `sha256HexPrefix` helper\n\nThe telephone is already in its normalized/stored form at that point (set earlier in `addOwner`), so the hash uses the canonical value.\n\n**Downstream values that build on `customerCode` moved automatically**, since they already read it:\n- `membershipNumber` \u2192 now `<REGION>-<HASH8>-M<YY>`\n- `checkDigit` (Luhn over digits in the code) \u2192 now computed over the new code's digits\n- the create audit record \u2192 logs the new `customerCode`\n\n**`OwnerMapper.locality(Owner)`** \u2014 moved to the new identity: it now returns the REGION component of the `customerCode` (the part before the first `-`), falling back to `CityRegionResolver` only when no `customerCode` is assigned (e.g. seed data).\n\nI also updated the javadoc examples on `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` to reflect the new format.",
